# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local development. No secret in this file
# is ever committed: the tenant id and the SAML metadata live only in the Entra
# and Clerk dashboards, and token verification needs no Clerk secret key.

# Written by `bun run convex` (convex dev). Leave it to the CLI.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=

# Clerk publishable key for this environment. Development instances issue
# pk_test_…; production issues pk_live_…. Not a secret — it ships in the bundle.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# The email domain the Clerk SAML enterprise connection is registered against
# (production only, e.g. vctusa.com). Setting it makes the sign-in button go
# straight to Microsoft with no email step. Leave it unset locally: development
# instances sign in with an email code, which needs no corporate IdP.
#
# Required wherever the publishable key is a live one (pk_live_…). A production
# build without it shows "Sign-in isn't configured" rather than the development
# widget, which a production Clerk instance would refuse anyway.
# VITE_CLERK_ENTERPRISE_DOMAIN=

# --- Convex deployment environment variables (NOT read from this file) -------
# Set on the deployment itself, per environment:
#
#   bunx convex env set CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN https://<slug>.clerk.accounts.dev
#   bunx convex env set CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN https://clerk.<domain> --prod
#
# It is Clerk's Frontend API URL, and must equal the token's `iss` exactly.
# Without it every call is anonymous and the backend denies everything.
